mode script

// Issue #326 reachability regression fixture: dyn dispatch on a LITERAL
// type name.
//
// `dyn_fn("I64", "to_str")` names its target completely at compile time, so
// the scavenger's root is the exact pair `I64.to_str` and the builder emits
// exactly one `_dyn` wrapper. That exact-pair path existed but never ran:
// only the METHOD argument was exempt from arg hoisting, so a literal TYPE
// name was hoisted into a pooled-Str temp and both readers saw an Ident
// instead of a literal, falling back to the `*.method` wildcard that keeps
// `to_str` on EVERY type -- including the compiler's own Expr/NodeType
// model, which is why this file used to emit 3,125 lines of C for four
// statements.
//
// The other fixtures cannot catch this: test/dyn_vecs.til and friends reach
// dyn dispatch through std/dyn_array, whose `dyn_fn(elem_type, "clone")`
// takes a RUNTIME type and so needs the wildcard by construction. Only a
// fully-literal call proves the exact pair works.
//
// dyn_literal_no_ast_model asserts the AST model is absent from the
// generated C; the `both` entry proves what survives still dispatches, in
// the interpreter (which resolves the pair by runtime name off the AST) as
// well as compiled.

to_str_fn : Dynamic = dyn_fn("I64", "to_str")

n : I64 = 42
println("dyn_literal ", n.to_str())
